            "id": "4650018",
            "title": "Eni and Repsol said to be weighing a partial sale of top Venezuela gas field",
            "description": "<html><body><p data-eci=\"true\">European energy groups Eni (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/E\" title=\"Eni S.p.A.\">E</a></span></span>) (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/EIPAF\" title=\"Eni S.p.A.\">EIPAF</a></span></span>) and Repsol (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/REPYY\" title=\"Repsol, S.A.\">REPYY</a></span></span>) are considering whether to sell a portion of their stakes in the Perla natural gas field off Venezuela’s coast, Bloomberg reported on Saturday, citing people familiar with the matter.</p>\n<p>The companies that currently own 50% each of the venture are seeking additional funds to help develop the massive offshore field, which they discovered in 2009 in the shallow waters close to Venezuela’s border with Colombia.</p>\n<p>Eni (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/E\" title=\"Eni S.p.A.\">E</a>) and Repsol (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/REPYY\" title=\"Repsol, S.A.\">REPYY</a>) are seeking a partial sale, the people said, asking for anonymity, as they are not authorized to discuss confidential information. Eni (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/E\" title=\"Eni S.p.A.\">E</a>) and Repsol (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/REPYF\" title=\"Repsol, S.A.\">REPYF</a></span></span>) didn’t respond to Bloomberg’s requests for comment.</p>\n<p>Perla is estimated to hold approximately 17T cubic feet of gas, making it one of the largest gas fields in Latin America.</p>\n<p>In April, the companies reached a deal with the Venezuelan government to begin natural gas exports from the oil-rich nation by the end of 2031. The agreement with the country’s interim president, Delcy Rodríguez, will enable the duo to more than double production at <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4576709-eni-repsol-plan-to-start-exporting-venezuelan-gas-by-2031-bloomberg\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">the Perla field.</a></p>\n</body></html>",
