            "id": "4649724",
            "title": "Earnings Scoreboard: all 8 S&P 500 firms beat EPS estimates, 6 saw profits rise Y/Y",
            "description": "<html><body><p class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\" data-eci=\"true\" data-end=\"391\" data-start=\"0\" dir=\"auto\">Corporate earnings for 8 S&amp;P 500 companies came out last week across different sectors: Carnival (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/CCL\" title=\"Carnival Corporation Ltd.\">CCL</a></span></span></span>), Micron Technology (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/MU\" title=\"Micron Technology, Inc.\">MU</a></span></span></span>), Conagra Brands (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/CAG\" title=\"Conagra Brands, Inc.\">CAG</a></span></span></span>), FactSet Research Systems (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/FDS\" title=\"FactSet Research Systems Inc.\">FDS</a></span></span>), Jabil (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/JBL\" title=\"Jabil Inc.\">JBL</a></span></span>), Accenture (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/ACN\" title=\"Accenture plc\">ACN</a></span></span></span>), McCormick &amp; Company (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/MKC\" title=\"McCormick &amp; Company, Incorporated\">MKC</a></span></span>), and NIKE (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/NKE\" title=\"NIKE, Inc.\">NKE</a></span></span></span>) were among the companies that gave their quarterly numbers.<span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchor\"></span></p>\n<p data-end=\"414\" data-start=\"393\" dir=\"auto\"><strong data-end=\"414\" data-start=\"393\">Earnings Roundup:</strong></p>\n<ul data-end=\"932\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\" data-start=\"416\">\n<li data-end=\"679\" data-section-id=\"eeapj2\" data-start=\"416\">\n<strong data-end=\"434\" data-start=\"418\">Bottom Line:</strong> Earnings performance was broadly positive, with all 8 reporting companies surpassing consensus EPS estimates and zero bottom-line misses. On a Y/Y basis, 6 of the 8 firms expanded profits, while Carnival's (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/CCL\" title=\"Carnival Corporation Ltd.\">CCL</a>) EPS was unchanged and Nike's (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/NKE\" title=\"NIKE, Inc.\">NKE</a>) declined.</li>\n<li data-end=\"932\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-section-id=\"lgq9il\" data-start=\"680\">\n<strong data-end=\"695\" data-start=\"682\">Top Line:</strong> Revenue results were also largely positive, with 7 companies topping Wall Street expectations and Nike (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/NKE\" title=\"NIKE, Inc.\">NKE</a>) falling short. Overall, 6 of the 8 firms achieved Y/Y revenue growth, while Conagra (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/CAG\" title=\"Conagra Brands, Inc.\">CAG</a>) and Nike (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/NKE\" title=\"NIKE, Inc.\">NKE</a>) reported lower revenue from a year earlier.</li>\n</ul>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<figure class=\"regular-img-figure\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span><img alt=\"Revenue and EPS\" data-caption=\"\" data-original-src=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/attachment/image/3b1ea05fae8fcb543553a31af729ed0e.png\" data-rel=\"lightbox\" data-source=\"Seeking Alpha\" fetchpriority=\"high\" height=\"204\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 36px), (max-width: 1023px) calc(100vw - 180px), 552px\" src=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/attachment/image/3b1ea05fae8fcb543553a31af729ed0e.png?io=w640\" srcset=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/attachment/image/3b1ea05fae8fcb543553a31af729ed0e.png?io=w750 750w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/attachment/image/3b1ea05fae8fcb543553a31af729ed0e.png?io=w640 640w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/attachment/image/3b1ea05fae8fcb543553a31af729ed0e.png?io=w480 480w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/attachment/image/3b1ea05fae8fcb543553a31af729ed0e.png?io=w320 320w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/attachment/image/3b1ea05fae8fcb543553a31af729ed0e.png?io=w240 240w\" width=\"900\"/></span><figcaption class=\"overlay-title\"><p class=\"item-caption\"><span class=\"item-source\">Seeking Alpha</span></p></figcaption></figure><p class=\"isSelectedEnd\">Carnival (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/CCL\" title=\"Carnival Corporation Ltd.\">CCL</a>) jumped after <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4648187-conagra-shares-inch-higher-after-quarterly-profit-tops-estimates\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Q3 results topped expectations\">Q3 results topped expectations</a>, with EPS of $1.43 beating consensus by $0.08. Strong bookings and continued demand helped the cruise operator raise its outlook.</p>\n<p class=\"isSelectedEnd\">Micron Technology (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/MU\" title=\"Micron Technology, Inc.\">MU</a>) stock increased after it delivered <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4648585-micron-slips-even-as-q4-results-guidance-top-estimates\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Q4 report\">Q4 report</a>, with EPS of $33.42 topping estimates by $1.60. Strong AI-driven memory demand helped drive the results, while the company’s outlook also came in well above expectations.</p>\n<p class=\"isSelectedEnd\">Conagra Brands (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/CAG\" title=\"Conagra Brands, Inc.\">CAG</a>) beat <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4648187-conagra-shares-inch-higher-after-quarterly-profit-tops-estimates\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Q1 profit expectations\">Q1 profit expectations</a>, with EPS of $0.41 coming in $0.13 above consensus. The food maker maintained its fiscal 2027 outlook despite a modest decline in sales.</p>\n<p class=\"isSelectedEnd\">FactSet Research Systems (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/FDS\" title=\"FactSet Research Systems Inc.\">FDS</a>) topped Q4 expectations, with EPS of $4.52 <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4648806-factset-expects-5-percent-to-6_5-percent-organic-asv-growth-in-fy-27-while-pointing-to-25-to\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"beating estimates\">beating estimates</a> by $0.17 as revenue rose 6.3% Y/Y. The company continued to benefit from growth in its subscription business.</p>\n<p class=\"isSelectedEnd\">Jabil (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/JBL\" title=\"Jabil Inc.\">JBL</a>) exceeded Q4 profit expectations, with EPS of $4.40 <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4648779-jabil-retreats-10-amid-fiscal-2027-outlook\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"beating consensus\">beating consensus</a> by $0.32. The electronics manufacturer pointed to continued strength across its business as it entered fiscal 2027.</p>\n<p class=\"isSelectedEnd\">Accenture (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/ACN\" title=\"Accenture plc\">ACN</a>) surged after <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4649308-accenture-expects-fy-2027-eps-of-14_39-to-14_81-as-it-plans-about-5b-of-acquisitions\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Q4 results beat expectations\">Q4 results beat expectations</a>, with EPS of $3.29 topping consensus by $0.11. The company also issued its fiscal 2027 outlook as demand for AI-related services remained strong.</p>\n<p class=\"isSelectedEnd\">McCormick &amp; Company (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/MKC\" title=\"McCormick &amp; Company, Incorporated\">MKC</a>) <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4648918-mccormick-rallies-after-seeing-organic-sales-growth-and-margin-expansion-in-fq3\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"beat Q3 profit expectations\">beat Q3 profit expectations</a>, with EPS of $0.86 topping consensus by $0.10. The company highlighted continued sales momentum and outlined plans to reduce debt.</p>\n<p>NIKE (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/NKE\" title=\"NIKE, Inc.\">NKE</a>)<span> <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4649510-nikes-turnaround-faces-more-headwinds-as-china-sales-slide-sees-further-sales-decline-in-fy27\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"beat Q1 EPS expectations\">beat Q1 EPS expectations</a>, but revenue fell 4.4% Y/Y to $11.21B, missing estimates by $106.06M. Weakness in sales kept pressure on the company's ongoing turnaround.</span></p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\" dir=\"auto\"><strong>Earnings next week:</strong></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Key reports to watch include Constellation Brands (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/STZ\" title=\"Constellation Brands, Inc.\">STZ</a></span></span>), PepsiCo (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/PEP\" title=\"PepsiCo, Inc.\">PEP</a></span></span>), and Delta Air Lines (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/DAL\" title=\"Delta Air Lines, Inc.\">DAL</a></span></span>).</p>\n</body></html>",
