            "id": "4649975",
            "title": "Crypto names slide the most; Brazilian banks dominate gainers in the week's financial movers",
            "description": "<html><body><p data-eci=\"true\">With bitcoin (BTC-US) remaining more or less stagnant over the week, trading at $84.4K late Friday afternoon, compared with $84.1K at on Sept. 25, crypto and blockchain-related stocks accounted for four of the five biggest financial decliners of the past week.</p>\n<p>Three of the biggest gainers were Brazilian banks ahead of the first round of the country's presidential election on Sunday.  The winner of the final round, which is set for later in the month, will get to fill vacancies in Brazil's Supreme Court, central bank, and economic regulators.</p>\n<p>For the week, the State Street Financial Select Sector SPDR ETF (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/XLF\" title=\"State Street Financial Sel Sec SPDR ETF\">XLF</a>) slipped 2.5% as Treasury yields continued to climb, underperforming the S&amp;P 500's (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/SP500\" title=\"S&amp;P 500 Index\">SP500</a>) 0.3% dip. For the past month, it dropped 7.3% compared with the S&amp;P's 0.1% increase.</p>\n<p>The decliners were led by Riot Platforms' (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/RIOT\" title=\"Riot Platforms, Inc.\">RIOT</a></span></span></span></span>) 14% drop for the week, followed by blockchain-focused firm Figure Technology's (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/FIGR\" title=\"Figure Technology Solutions, Inc.\">FIGR</a></span></span></span></span>) 11% decline.</p>\n<p>MARA Holdings (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/MARA\" title=\"MARA Holdings, Inc.\">MARA</a></span></span></span></span>) stock, one of the most <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4649813-ondas-tops-technology-stocks-in-short-interest-ubiquiti-sees-the-lowest-exposure\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"shorted tech stocks\">shorted tech stocks</a>, slid 11%. </p>\n<p>Piper Sandler (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/PIPR\" title=\"Piper Sandler Companies\">PIPR</a></span></span></span></span>) fell 9.7%, retreating from a surge on Tuesday following a report that it <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4648058-perella-weinberg-surges-on-report-piper-sandler-in-talks-to-acuire\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"entered talks\">entered talks</a> with Perella Weinberg (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/PWP\" title=\"Perella Weinberg Partners\">PWP</a>) about a possible sale.</p>\n<p>Stablecoin issuer Circle Internet (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/CRCL\" title=\"Circle Internet Group, Inc.\">CRCL</a></span></span></span></span>) slipped 8.7% for the week.</p>\n<p>On the opposite side of the performance spectrum, Virtu Financial (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/VIRT\" title=\"Virtu Financial, Inc.\">VIRT</a></span></span></span></span>) scored the biggest gain of the week, rising 10%. Early in the week, it announced the launch of a<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/pr/20665327-virtu-financial-announces-launch-of-block-crossing-for-equity-securities-listed-on-the-saudi\" target=\"_blank\" title=\" block-trading indications network \"> block-trading indications network </a>for equity securities listed on the Saudi Exchange.</p>\n<p>Brazilian banks took the next three spots, with Inter &amp; Co. (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/INTR\" title=\"Inter &amp; Co, Inc.\">INTR</a></span></span></span></span>) rising 7.2%, Banco Bradesco (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/BBD\" title=\"Banco Bradesco S.A.\">BBD</a></span></span></span></span>) gaining 7.0%, and Itaú Unibanco Holding (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/ITUB\" title=\"Itaú Unibanco Holding S.A.\">ITUB</a></span></span></span></span>) climbing 5.9%.</p>\n<p>HCI Group (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/HCI\" title=\"HCI Group, Inc.\">HCI</a></span></span></span></span>), a property &amp; casualty insurance business, rounded out the top five with a 5.3% increase for the week.</p>\n</body></html>",
