            "id": "4649994",
            "title": "Notable tech headlines for the week: Micron, Nvidia, Accenture in focus",
            "description": "<html><body><p class=\"MsoNormal\" data-eci=\"true\">The tech sector remained in the spotlight this week as investors assessed headlines from top companies including Micron, AMD and Accenture.</p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">The tech-focused Nasdaq Composite Index (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/COMP:IND\" title=\"NASDAQ Composite Index\">COMP:IND</a>) closed in the green on Friday. The Technology Select Sector SPDR Fund (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/XLK\" title=\"State Street Technology Select Sector SPDR ETF\">XLK</a></span></span>) rose over 1% during the week. The top S&amp;P 500 technology gainers and losers for the last week are as follows:</p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong>Top Gainers:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Lumentum (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/LITE\" title=\"Lumentum Holdings Inc.\">LITE</a></span></span>) +15.27%</li>\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Synopsys (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/SNPS\" title=\"Synopsys, Inc.\">SNPS</a></span></span>) +15.06%</li>\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Coherent (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/COHR\" title=\"Coherent Corp.\">COHR</a></span></span>) +13.93%</li>\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Accenture (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/ACN\" title=\"Accenture plc\">ACN</a></span></span>) +12.94%</li>\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Teradyne (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/TER\" title=\"Teradyne, Inc.\">TER</a></span></span>) +12.72%</li>\n</ul>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong>Top Losers:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Fair Issac (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/FICO\" title=\"Fair Isaac Corporation\">FICO</a></span></span>) -23.39%</li>\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Global Payments (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/GPN\" title=\"Global Payments Inc.\">GPN</a></span></span>) -9.38%</li>\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Western Digital (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/WDC\" title=\"Western Digital Corporation\">WDC</a></span></span>) -9.09%</li>\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Qualcomm (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/QCOM\" title=\"QUALCOMM Incorporated\">QCOM</a></span></span>) -8.47%</li>\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Fidelity National Information Services (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/FIS\" title=\"Fidelity National Information Services, Inc.\">FIS</a></span></span>) -8.39%</li>\n</ul>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong>Here are some of the important technology stories from this week:</strong></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong>Nvidia unveils massive $150B increase to share buyback program</strong></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Nvidia (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/NVDA\" title=\"NVIDIA Corporation\">NVDA</a></span></span>) said its board of directors has increased the size of its buyback program by <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4647498-nvidia-unveils-massive-150b-increase-to-share-buyback-program\">$150B</a>, using its massive balance sheet to buy back its stock. The $150B increase leaves Nvidia with $235B in buyback authorization. It is the largest buyback program in U.S. history, according to data compiled by Bloomberg.</p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong>AMD to acquire World Labs in $8.2B all-stock deal</strong></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Advanced Micro Devices (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/AMD\" title=\"Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.\">AMD</a></span></span>) <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4647774-amd-to-acquire-world-labs-in-82b-all-stock-deal\">said</a> it would acquire World Labs, an AI model and research lab, in an all-stock transaction is valued at nearly $8.2 billion.</p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">The surprise announcement was praised by analysts from Wall Street. Citi analyst Atif Malik said the decision to add World Labs and its founder, Fei-Fei Li (widely referred to as the “godmother of AI”), gives the company “deeper visibility” into how AI models are evolving.</p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">RBC analyst Srini Pajjuri echoed those sentiments, suggesting that the deal to acquire the privately held AI research lab could \"help position the company to offer full-stack solutions for robotics, simulation, and physical AI markets, which are in early stages.\"</p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong>Micron, Accenture quarterly results impressed investors </strong></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Micron Technology (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/MU\" title=\"Micron Technology, Inc.\">MU</a></span></span>) demonstrated durability in its fourth-quarter <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4648734-micron-non-gaap-eps-of-33_42-beats-by-1_60-revenue-of-54_23b-beats-by-2_76b#source=section%3Amain_content%7Cbutton%3Abody_link%7Cfirst_level_url%3Anews\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"earnings results\">earnings results</a> and outlook as its strategic customer agreements, or SCAs, continued to increase. As a result, analysts continue to see upside for the stock, which has already more than sextupled over the past year.</p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Similarly, investors were impressed after Accenture (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/ACN\" title=\"Accenture plc\">ACN</a>) reported fiscal quarterly results that exceeded expectations on both revenue and bookings. Shares closed nearly 16% on Thursday.</p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">In other news,<strong> HPE</strong> (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/HPE\" title=\"Hewlett Packard Enterprise Company\">HPE</a></span></span>) closed nearly 4% higher on Wednesday after the company <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/pr/20669008-hpe-secures-its-first-amd-helios-order-in-1_2-billion-deal-with-vultr#source=section%3Amain_content%7Cbutton%3Abody_link%7Cfirst_level_url%3Anews\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"said\">said</a> it won a $1.2B order of AMD's (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/AMD\" title=\"Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.\">AMD</a>) Helios AI rack from cloud infrastructure company Vultr. The company also increased its outlook for 2027, citing gains in networking.</p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">The company now sees networking growth in fiscal 2027 in the high-teens to low-20s on a percentage basis as it is gaining share in the data center networking market. Data center networking revenue is expected to grow at a low-to-high 50s percent compound annual rate through fiscal 2029.</p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong>Anthropic</strong> (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/ANTHRO\" title=\"Anthropic\">ANTHRO</a>) intends to <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4649302-anthropic-plans-to-go-public-before-thanksgiving-report\">launch</a> its initial public offering before the Thanksgiving holiday begins, according to Bloomberg.</p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">As per another Bloomberg News report, <strong>Broadcom's</strong> (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/AVGO\" title=\"Broadcom Inc.\">AVGO</a></span></span>) Wall Street syndicate is starting to gather $60B of fresh AI chip financing to benefit Anthropic PBC and other companies.</p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong>Meta Platforms</strong> (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/META\" title=\"Meta Platforms, Inc.\">META</a></span></span>) is adding an entirely new platform to target organizations, Meta Enterprise Platform, and the social media giant has <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4647538-mongodb-tumbles-after-ceo-desai-suddenly-steps-down-for-meta-role#source=section%3Amain_content%7Cbutton%3Abody_link%7Cfirst_level_url%3Anews\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"tapped\">tapped</a> MongoDB (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/MDB\" title=\"MongoDB, Inc.\">MDB</a></span></span>) CEO Chirantan “CJ” Desai to lead the effort. The company also <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4647873-meta-extends-muse-ai-push-with-new-small-business-capabilities\">introduced</a> Muse for Small Business, expanding its AI agent with new skills and app connections designed to help small businesses manage their operations.</p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> </p>\n</body></html>",
